audit = f"# Full-tangent execution audit v283M\n\nFinal classification: `{r['classification']}`. Source/provenance, exact historical reproduction, implementation invariants, primary inference, secondary probes and final scientific checks completed.\n\n## Integrity and source binding\n\n- Preregistration SHA256: `{r['preregistration_sha256']}`; unchanged from the supplied launch archive.\n- Stage 0 recorded UTC/Asia-Shanghai times, Python/PyTorch/macOS versions, device availability and repository commit/status before full-tangent outcomes.\n- {len(man['entries'])} source bindings passed, including every response source, router checkpoint, geometry cache and run metadata file for all 64 primary records, model configs and weight assets, construction code and protocols.\n- S1 revision a39f36b100fe8a5377810d56c3f4789b9c53ac42, measured layer 3, d=512,D=2048; S2 revision 28e66ca6931668447a3bac213f23d990ad3b0e2b, layer 19,d=576,D=1536.\n- Eight prescribed seeds per family, g=1,2,4,8, exactly 64,000-token checkpoints, 2,048 documents and 12,288 ordered pairs, 1,024 pairs in each of 12 ordered domain groups. All cache pair indices were verified against document-ID manifests.\n- Output placement follows the user's AGENTS.md default under the current Codex project's outputs. The example research-root output path in the attachment was not used. Historical sources and manuscript v283M were read-only.\n\n## Child parameter blocks and kernels\n\nEXPERT_BLOCK_BINDING_v283M.json/.md was written before new full-tangent outcome computation. The preserved module constructors verified identical child geometry across four independent parent copies. S1 contains up.weight, up.bias and down.weight; the output bias is used once as a common term and is excluded. S2 contains gate_proj.weight, up_proj.weight and down_proj.weight. Copied down columns are multiplied by g in both families.\n\nThe optimized float64 kernel contracts the output-projection feature inner product and input-parameter derivative terms. GELU's input bias adds one to h_x dot h_y. SwiGLU uses both gate and up derivatives. No Jacobian or full NTK matrix was materialized. Full geometry was computed once per family × g and reused across all seeds.\n\nThe fixed autograd subset spans both families, g=2/g=8 and first/last child: eight cases. Each reference sums scalar-output gradient inner products across all d outputs. Maximum full-kernel absolute error = {num(checks['max_full_abs_error'])}; maximum relative error = {num(checks['max_full_relative_error'])}. Output-only optimized/autograd maximum absolute error = {num(checks['max_output_abs_error'])}. The same-feature historical output-only identity independently passes.\n\nThe first audit attempt conflated a float64/float32 feature comparison with the output-projection invariant. It was corrected before primary coordinates, without changing the frozen subset, thresholds, expert block, metric or protocol. The original attempt and all cross-precision diagnostics remain archived. Maximum cross-precision historical feature bridge difference = {num(checks['max_historical_restriction_abs_error'])}; this is not a claim of exact equality between different arithmetic precisions. A NumPy-scalar JSON serialization error was also repaired before primary computation.\n\n## Historical reproduction and numerical floors\n\nAll 64 historical response records were recomputed using the original MPS float32 operations followed by CPU float64 aggregation. Maximum B-coordinate error = 0; maximum P_B error = 0. Recomputed feature geometry matches the preserved geometry. g=1 coordinates and powers are exact zero.\n\nFull-kernel cross-check discrepancies were conservatively propagated using per-domain mean L1 norms of q_C and an extra factor four. NUMERICAL_FLOORS_FREEZE_v283M.json was written before primary response coordinates. tau_P=max(1e-20,100 epsilon_B^2)=1e-20 in every cell. The sign comparison uses fixed within-cell floors max(1e-10, propagated error), with the 1e-10 floor tied to the square root of the structural power floor. All 288 nontrivial coordinates in each family remain sign-eligible.\n\n## Frozen H0/H1/H2/H3/H4\n\n- H0: PASS in both families, exact g=1 structural zero.\n- H1: PASS in all six nontrivial cells, 8/8 seeds each above the frozen threshold (required 7/8).\n- H2: S1 passes all confirmation criteria. S2 fails the Spearman and sign-agreement confidence-bound criteria. All family-level point estimates meet the positive-association condition for PARTIAL_CHANNEL_AGREEMENT.\n- H3: all six cells reported below; diagnostics are retained regardless of sign. S2 g=2 has weak/slightly negative association.\n- H4: PASS in both families and all g. Maximum A/M-to-C geometry power ratio = {num(maxleak)} versus 1e-10 tolerance; g=1 geometry powers are exactly zero.\n\n{metrics_table()}\n{cell_table()}\n## Inference and independent verification\n\n20,000 whole-seed bootstrap draws use PCG64(2026101201). Both families are reported separately, without a pooled upgrade. RMS normalization is re-estimated per family × g within each bootstrap draw. Bootstrap indices and full distributions are included.\n\n{ver['checks_passed']} final scientific checks passed. An independent scalar Python-statistics implementation verified the primary cosine/Pearson/Spearman/sign metrics and six fixed bootstrap draws per family, including tie-average ranks and the per-cell-normalized slope. Pair-level stored contributions reproduce all 768 signed coordinates, confidence intervals match saved distributions, source hashes were rechecked, and the primary result hash was unchanged by secondary computation.\n\n## Secondary and optional work\n\nPrimary classification was persisted with its hash before Stage 7. Four orthonormal output probes per family use sequential PCG64(2026101202) Gaussian d×4 matrices and float64 reduced QR (S1 then S2). All 3,072 directional coordinates and 24 nontrivial cell diagnostics are stored separately. Direction-specific family cosine ranges: S1 {num(min((z['cosine'] for z in sec['families']['S1'])))} to {num(max((z['cosine'] for z in sec['families']['S1'])))}; S2 {num(min((z['cosine'] for z in sec['families']['S2'])))} to {num(max((z['cosine'] for z in sec['families']['S2'])))}. Negative associations occur. Secondary results do not change the primary label.\n\nThe optional background-mode-conversion extension was omitted. It is outside the frozen primary decision; historical successful mode-conversion artifacts and interpretations remain unchanged.\n\n## Manuscript and archive\n\nA v284M scope-narrowing update is not warranted. An optional future manuscript version may report this partial benchmark with the qualifications in MANUSCRIPT_PATCH_FULL_TANGENT_v283M.md. The scientific-impact file explicitly answers the six required questions. The completion archive includes new coordinate/geometry/bootstrap artifacts and source snapshots. External source-bound model and historical caches are listed rather than duplicated. Output checksums, archive verification and read-only completion protect the completed run against accidental edits.\n"
(OUT / 'FULL_TANGENT_AUDIT_v283M.md').write_text(audit)
summary = f"# Full-tangent benchmark v283M — execution summary\n\n最终分类：`{r['classification']}`。\n\n225 项来源哈希与 64 条主记录通过核验；历史 B/P_B 复现误差为零。全切线解析/自动微分最大绝对误差 {num(checks['max_full_abs_error'])}、相对误差 {num(checks['max_full_relative_error'])}；输出投影同特征恒等式通过。跨精度桥接差异及修正记录完整保留于审计。\n\nH0、H1、H4 全通过；H2：S1 满足全部确认条件，S2 的 Spearman 及符号一致率置信下界未达标准；H3 六个单元完整报告。20,000 次整种子 bootstrap 的结果如下。\n\n{metrics_table()}\n{cell_table()}\n四个正交方向探针已另行报告，不改变主分类。最终 {ver['checks_passed']} 项独立科学验证通过。未修改历史数据或稿件 v283M。不支持收窄一般 B_ts 的范围声明，因此不要求升级稿件；v284M 若新增本结果，只能报告“部分一致”。\n\n归档：../PhysicsForAI_Project1_FullTangentBenchmark_v283M_r1.tar.gz；SHA256 校验文件同目录。审计、科学影响、建议稿、CSV/JSON、源码和所有新缓存均包含在归档中。\n"
